            explanationEn: 'James\'s central criticism. Wundt saw consciousness as composed of "atoms", basic sensations that could be isolated and studied. James argued that this is a fundamental mistake: <strong>consciousness does not break into parts, it flows continuously.</strong> His metaphor: not a train of carriages, but a river.',
