            explanationEn: 'This was the birth <strong>of functional psychology.</strong> James did not ask "made of what?" but "for what purpose?", how does consciousness serve us? How does it help us survive, plan, cope? Instead of breaking consciousness into components, he wanted to understand its functions. This approach influenced all the psychology that came after him, from Skinner to modern cognitive science.',
