            explanationEn: 'One of Freud\'s radical ideas: the <strong>body expresses what the mind cannot say. Physical symptoms, headaches, dizziness, partial paralysis, can be an expression of drives or feelings that the mind rejects from awareness. The body</strong> does not lie, but it speaks in a different language. Psychoanalysis offers a way to translate that language back into words.',
