            explanationEn: 'The great argument that caused their separation. <strong>Freud: the unconscious is a private accumulation of repressed contents from your childhood.</strong> Jung: there is a personal unconscious, but also a deeper layer, *shared by all human beings. This layer, the collective unconscious, contains archetypes, ancient mental patterns that reveal themselves in dreams, in myths, and in symbols.',
