            explanationEn: 'A central concept for Jung. Individuation is not "being an individual" in the superficial sense. It is an inner process of <strong>unification: to know your shadow, your anima/animus, your unconscious parts, and to connect them to the conscious self. The goal:</strong> to become a whole, unified person. Unlike Freud, who saw the psyche as an arena of conflicts, Jung saw it as a journey toward the center, toward your true self.',
