            explanationEn: 'Skinner\'s central position. Not that he denied the existence of thoughts, but that he argued they cannot be studied scientifically. All the hypotheses about "the unconscious," "archetypes," "complexes" are untestable. What can be studied, is behavior. What a person does, how he responds, how consequences change his behavior. Only that can be real science.',
