            explanationEn: 'Skinner\'s fundamental principle. <strong>Behavior is controlled by its consequences</strong>. If an action leads to positive reinforcement, it will repeat itself. If it leads to punishment, it will disappear. He proved this in the laboratory with pigeons and rats, but argued that the same principle applies to human beings. Everything we are, according to Skinner, is the result of the history of our reinforcements.',
