            contentEn: 'But there is one question that almost all of our thinkers answered <strong>indirectly, what drives a person?</strong></p><p>Freud and Jung said: unconscious drives. Skinner said: reinforcements from the environment. Rogers said: an actualizing tendency.</p><p><strong>But through modern eyes, none of these answers alone is sufficient. Why</strong> does one person fight for survival while another devotes his life to creation? Why does one chase money while another chases meaning?</p><p><strong>This is the question of Chapter 2: what drives us?</strong> And in it we will meet Adler, Maslow, Frankl, Fromm and others, each with a different answer, each one essential.',
